(version 1)

; Seatbelt profile: run `betterleaks` fully offline. Nothing this process
; does can reach the network, no matter what flags/config get passed to it
; (including --validation, which normally calls out to live provider APIs).
;
; Everything else is allowed - this only isolates network access, not the
; filesystem or anything else. betterleaks needs to run whatever toolchain
; resolves it on PATH (a plain binary, a Homebrew symlink, a version
; manager shim, ...) without the sandbox caring what that is or where it
; lives, so file access is unrestricted.

(allow default)

(deny network*)
(deny network-inbound)
(deny network-outbound)
